{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-flat-connection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-flat-connection","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Flat connection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-local-system"],"tags":["geometric-langlands","connection","q-deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QFlatConnection","text":"q-flat-connection.md","leanSource":"q-flat-connection.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-flat-connection\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable\nuniverse and let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{V}</code> be a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q</code>-equivariant object in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> over the\nbrane curve <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code>.  A <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-flat connection</strong> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{V}</code> is a\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-connection\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_q \\colon \\mathcal{V} \\to \\Omega^1_q \\otimes \\mathcal{V}</code>\n(<a href=\"#def:categorical-q-connection\">categorical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-connection</a>)\nwhose total curvature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_q^2</code> equals the intrinsic\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-curvature determined by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\nabla_q^2 = (q - 1)\\mathcal{F}_q^{\\mathrm{intr}}.</code></pre>\n<p>Here, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{F}_q^{\\mathrm{intr}} \\in \\mathrm{End}(\\mathcal{V}) \\otimes \\Omega^2_q</code> is the <strong>intrinsic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-curvature</strong>, defined as the image of the obstruction class <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_0</code> under the Hochschild--Kostant--Rosenberg map (<a href=\"#rem:kummer-filtration-obstruction\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting-kummer-motivic\">Kummer filtration</a>):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{F}_q^{\\mathrm{intr}}\n  = \n  \\mathrm{HKR}^{-1}(\\kappa_0)\n   \\in \n  HH^2(\\mathcal{U}_q, \\mathrm{Ad}).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-flat-connection.md","heading":"Definition","number":"24.2.3","page":"b/def-q-flat-connection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QFlatConnection","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-flat-connection.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
